# Operator config for `make release server`. Not secrets — these only name
# which GCP project and terraform state bucket the rollout targets. The actual
# runtime secrets (admin token, session pepper, database URL) are generated by
# terraform and live in Secret Manager; nothing on this machine holds them.
#
#   cp deploy.env.example deploy.env
#   # fill in, then: make release server
#
# deploy.env is gitignored. The Makefile `include`s it, so use plain
# KEY=value lines — no `export`, no quotes, no shell expansion. Anything you
# pass on the make command line wins over this file.
#
# Not used by `make release web`: the Netlify build needs no configuration
# beyond netlify.toml, and the browser bundle takes no env vars at all.

# Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# The GCP project that owns Cloud Run, Cloud SQL and Artifact Registry.
GCP_PROJECT_ID=

# GCS bucket holding terraform remote state, conventionally
# <PROJECT_ID>-terraform-state. See server/DEPLOYMENT.md §1.
TF_STATE_BUCKET=

# Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Region for Cloud Run and Artifact Registry. Leave it unset: MUT-523 takes each project's region from
# config/gcp.json (europe-west1 for mtb3a-production, me-west1 for malafat-production), and deploy.sh and
# preflight refuse a GCP_REGION that disagrees with it.
# GCP_REGION=

# Who server commands from THIS checkout act as (MUT-523). mtb3a-production belongs to barmajiyatltd@gmail.com,
# which runs the move and its releases. Set both or neither. They apply to `make` and the scripts it runs only:
# gcloud gets CLOUDSDK_CORE_ACCOUNT, Terraform, cloud-sql-proxy and the client libraries get
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS. Nothing machine-wide changes, so other checkouts and sessions keep the machine's
# default gcloud account and ADC. The account must be in `gcloud auth list`; make the credentials file once as
# server/DEPLOYMENT.md §6d C0 says (application-default login into a temporary CLOUDSDK_CONFIG, then copy the file).
# Run project-move.sh or restore-drill.sh by hand with the same two exported in that terminal.
# GCP_ACCOUNT=barmajiyatltd@gmail.com
# GCP_ADC_FILE=~/.config/gcloud/adc-barmajiyatltd.json

# Artifact Registry repository name. Default: mutaba3a.
# ARTIFACT_REPO=mutaba3a

# Tag a fresh build with this name instead of the commit's short sha; it also
# lets a dirty tree through (the image is labelled dirty=true). Never an
# existing tag: deploy.sh refuses to push over one (MUT-347). To roll back, use
# make rollback-server SHA=<sha|api-vX.Y.Z> instead (server/DEPLOYMENT.md §6).
# IMAGE_TAG=

# Skip every terraform apply prompt. Only once you trust the plan.
# AUTO_APPROVE=1

# Local port for the Cloud SQL Auth Proxy during `prisma migrate deploy`.
# PROXY_PORT=5440

# Terraform environment; only `production` has a tfvars file today.
# ENVIRONMENT=production

# The PostHog project key (phc_…) for the portal's opt-in anonymous usage
# counts (MUT-155, ADR-090). Baked into dist-hosted at build time; it is a
# public ingest key, not a secret, but keep it out of git all the same. Left
# empty, the portal never asks and never sends. Never set this in CI.
# MUTABA3A_POSTHOG_KEY=

# The portal's Sentry DSN, mutaba3a-web project (MUT-149, ADR-091 am.11):
# crash reports from signed-in pages only. Public (it ships in the bundle), so
# not a secret, but kept out of git. It must be on the org's EU ingest host,
# the one PORTAL_CSP allows, or the build fails. Left empty, the portal reports
# nothing. With it set, the release also needs the source-map upload token:
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN in your shell, or once in the Keychain (DEPLOYMENT.md §1.5
# step 3). Never put that token in this file.
# MUTABA3A_SENTRY_DSN=

# The production Cloudflare Turnstile widget's SITE key (MUT-368): the bot
# check on the portal's /signup and /recover. Public (it ships in the bundle),
# never the secret (that is mutaba3a-api-turnstile-secret in Secret Manager).
# Left empty, builds carry Cloudflare's always-pass test key; deploy.sh refuses
# that once mailer = "resend". The build refuses anything shaped like a secret.
# MUTABA3A_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
